 "pages": "ads1278.pdf p.6-7 (pins, Table 1), p.4-5 (IOVDD/DVDD), p.8 (SPI timing), p.26 (Tables 8, 9), p.29 (sync, power-down), p.30-31 (Table 14, SPI interface, DRDY, TDM Figure 77), p.25 (data format, Table 5)",
 "notModeled": [
  "analog inputs, VCOM output, test mode TEST[1:0], modulator output mode (FORMAT = 110)",
  "the bus is the SPI, TDM fixed-position format (FORMAT[2:0] = 001) on DOUT1 with no CS: each DRDY falling edge starts a 192-bit frame of channels 1..8 in order (Figure 77); the dynamic-position TDM, discrete (per-channel DOUTn) and frame-sync formats are not modeled, the FORMAT pins are not read, DOUT2..DOUT8 are not driven",
  "daisy-chain: the data shifted in on DIN after the last channel are not passed through (idle 0)",
  "per-channel power-down PWDNn (powered-down channels read zero in fixed-position TDM, which the 0 V code already is) and the all-channels-down microwatt state (DRDY forced high)",
  "SYNC pin (filter restart, 129-conversion settling) and the DRDY hold-off of 129 conversions after a MODE change",
  "conversion time = 1 / data rate at fCLK = 27 MHz (the SPI-format maximum), CLKDIV = 1 (Table 8): high-speed 256 tCLK (105469 SPS), high-resolution and low-power 512 tCLK (52734 SPS), low-speed 2560 tCLK (10547 SPS); 37 MHz high-speed (frame-sync only), other CLK frequencies and CLKDIV are not modeled; the CLK pin is not used",
  "DRDY returns high on the first SCLK falling edge (modeled as cleared on reading the data); the high pulse before the next conversion when data are not read",
  "HFQ (CFP-84) pin names follow the pin table (the drawing prints SYNCn, PWDNnN and RDYN/FSYNC)"
 ],
 "variants": "ADS1274 (4 channels) shares ads1278.pdf; ADS1278-EP (ads1278-ep.pdf, ADS1278MPAPTEP, PAP) and ADS1278-HT (ads1278-ht.pdf, ADS1278HPAP / ADS1278SHFQ; HFQ 84-pin ceramic package with the same functions, CLKDIV 1 = 32.768 MHz high-speed) are the same chip",
